This is a known issue introduced in Next.js 15.5.x when running as **standalone** in production. The root cause is the **`proxyClientMaxBodySize`** config that was added in 15.5 — it defaults to **1MB** and silently truncates/drops binary data from the request body before it reaches your Server Action.

## Root Cause

Next.js 15.5+ added an internal proxy layer for handling Server Action requests in standalone mode. This proxy has its own body size limit separate from `serverActions.bodySizeLimit`. When a file exceeds this proxy limit, the binary data is **silently dropped** — which is exactly the behavior you're seeing:
- File metadata (name, type) is preserved ✅
- Binary content is dropped → 0 bytes ❌
- Only happens in production (standalone) — not in dev ✅
- Larger files fail more reliably ✅

## Fix: Set `proxyClientMaxBodySize` in `next.config`

```js
// next.config.js
module.exports = {
  experimental: {
    proxyClientMaxBodySize: '50mb', // match or exceed your serverActions.bodySizeLimit
  },
  serverActions: {
    bodySizeLimit: '35mb',
  },
}
```

Docs: https://nextjs.org/docs/app/api-reference/config/next-config-js/proxyClientMaxBodySize

> **Important:** `proxyClientMaxBodySize` and `serverActions.bodySizeLimit` are separate limits. Both must be set large enough to handle your upload size.

## If you also use Middleware

If you have middleware that handles or passes through requests, there's a separate limit:

```js
// next.config.js
module.exports = {
  experimental: {
    proxyClientMaxBodySize: '50mb',
    middlewareClientMaxBodySize: '50mb', // if middleware is in the path
  },
  serverActions: {
    bodySizeLimit: '35mb',
  },
}
```

Docs: https://nextjs.org/docs/15/app/api-reference/config/next-config-js/middlewareClientMaxBodySize

## Why it's intermittent

The 50% failure rate at 150KB might seem odd given a 1MB default, but the proxy limit applies to the **entire request body** — including all FormData fields combined. If your form sends other fields alongside the file, the total can exceed the limit even for medium-sized files. Also, chunked upload behavior in browsers can vary, causing intermittent failures near the threshold.

## Related discussion

See also #89404 (raised by @lkho) which covers the same `proxyClientMaxBodySize` issue in more detail.

Setting `proxyClientMaxBodySize` to match your `bodySizeLimit` should fully resolve this.

