First you need to find where window is being accessed. Try this:

```js
// add this at the top of next.config.js or your custom server file
if (typeof window === 'undefined') {
  global.window = new Proxy({}, {
    get(target, prop) {
      console.trace(`window.${String(prop)} accessed on server`);
      return undefined;
    }
  });
}
```

This will print a stack trace every time something tries to access window on the server, so you can see exactly which module is the culprit.

---

Also try running with source maps enabled to get more accurate error locations:

```bash
NODE_OPTIONS='--enable-source-maps' node .next/standalone/server.js
```

